Let\'92s work through the position interface screen and how bearings are used to estimate positions. There shouldn\'92t be a finite time limit on the bearings that should be used to in the triangulation step. There should be a list in reverse chronological order (newest at the top) that allows users to select which to use. There needs to be a select/deselect all option. The bearings should be displayed above the list (as is done now) on a map, but the map should have a similar interface to the regular map screen with the ability to switch maps types, pan, zoom, and  measure distance. The bearings to the tag on the map should be selectable by clicking on them to include them or exclude them in the positioning analysis like they are in the list. Excluded bearings should still be seen on the map but translucent so the user knows they are there and can reselect them if needed. 
\f1\fs26 The position screen doesn\'92t currently show a map, allow panning or zooming. Also in that screen there are warnings that sometimes expand to a point where I can\'92t see the bearings to select.
