\f1\fs26 \cf0 {\listtext	1.	}\strike \strikec0 Bearing, positions, and other recordings aren\'92t updating on the map when added or deleted. I have to close and reopen the app to get them update.\strike0\striked0 \
{\listtext	2.	}\strike \strikec0 Bearings positions and other recordings should be selectable on the map with the info on them showing up at the bottom of the screen with the edit option. For positions there should be an option to show/hide the error ellipse and highlight which bearing were used to create the position. \
{\listtext	3.	}The + button and the map source bar at the bottom on the map and the lat/lon bar at the bottom of the map are overlapping. Fix it.\strike0\striked0 \
{\listtext	4.	}\strike \strikec0 There should be a live viewshed option that calculated the viewshed from the current user GPS position so that users can see it update as they are driving.\strike0\striked0 \
{\listtext	5.	}Feature for phase 2: allow users to select a driving path by picking point along a road and then calculate the scanned viewshed for that drive if there were scanning continuously while driving or the app would calculate the places along the route to stop and scan to maximize covered area for the drive.\
{\listtext	6.	}\strike \strikec0 There is still an M on the compass needle but that isn\'92t the magnetic north bearing. Remove the M\
{\listtext	7.	}The bubble level seems to move in the wrong direction when perturbed in  pitch direction but the correct direction in the roll direction when held near level\
{\listtext	8.	}The compass should show the location-based computed declination and allow the user to update manually. When the declination has been updated, it should be clearly noted on the compass and bearing measurement tool and confirm the user wants to continue to use to manually adjusted declination.\
{\listtext	9.	}The map selector at the top of the screen has terrain street and satellite. The terrain and satellite buttons have now margin to the edges of the screen. There should be a little space between the edge of the buttons and the screen edge. \
{\listtext	10.	}I like the clear  terrain street satellite buttons you made for the position map so that we can see the map behind the terrain street satellite buttons - can we use that same style on the main map so the map extends up further on the screen?\strike0\striked0 \
{\listtext	11.	}\strike \strikec0 Think this thru: do we need a \'93record\'94 button at the bottom of the map page if we have a + button on the map that does the same thing? I think we only need the + button.\
{\listtext	12.	}On the record screen has the directional, omnidirectional buttons below the tag. That should be at the top of the screen as the record type and should also include a \'93Note\'94 record type for general notes without the radio options and just includes the tag selector to tie a note to a tag. Notes records should include all the regular position information of other record types.\
{\listtext	13.	}There needs to be another record type for \'93No Signal\'94 that allows the user to select multiple tags from the list to record that they didn\'92t pick up a tag. Many times we scan multiple frequencies and pick up nothing. We need to be able to record what we didn\'92t hear quickly. \strike0\striked0 \
{\listtext	\strike \strikec0 14.	}\strikec0 The tag selector on the record screens should have a \'93Add new tag\'94 option that brings the user to the tag input screen if they roll to it and release. \
{\listtext	15.	}Previously Bearings on the map display only show a line so you know from what end it was measured. The position where it was measured should be marked with a circle with the existing bearing line coming out of the circle. There should be a translucent wedge in for bearing measurement that display in the map that shows the uncertainty measured for the bearing\
{\listtext	16.	}When recording a bearing or omnidirectional record, there should be a \'93preview\'94 button that takes the user to the map to see the bearing. There should be some way for them to move the bearing position manually in this screen in cases where the gps position is wrong. This can happen in canyons and in dense forest when there is GPS multipath. Don\'92t forget to have a back arrow on the preview screen to take them back to the standard record screen. This is somewhat address currently with the manual pin option but no one wants to manually enter a lat/lon. Just bring up the map and let the user select the point. This should work for the note and no signal types as well. \
{\listtext	17.	}Check the on off logic on the check boxes in the layers button in the map view. They don\'92t seem to consistently turn on and off when I select the checks boxes and the items they are supposed to hide and turn back on don\'92t seem to turn on.\
{\listtext	18.	}We Need more graduations for the vertical and horizontal direction with faint grey lines in the elevation graphs for the line segment measurement. The resolution should adapt to the map height and width for readability and resolution\strike0\striked0 .\
{\listtext	19.	}In the record screen (bearing mode), make the tag selector smaller so it doesn\'92t take up as much vertical space (maybe enough to show 3 tags. Move the peak/null to the advanced settings. Make the bearing quality, and pulse type (regular, mortality), and signal strength rollers that are adjacent and on the screen at the same vertical position but keep their colors. We want to make room for doing bearing measurements right from the record screen. We want all the standard options simultaneously visible without scrolling except for the advanced, notes, preview/set, attached to triangulation which the user can scroll to. This makes it so that the users don\'92t typically have to scroll to make a recording. The add a point and range bearing recording buttons on this screen with a live bearing displayed in the bearing box until the user records the button. The \'91point\'92 button should click and stay on to hold the current bearing, going from light green to dark green when holding. The bearing then would be fixed in the box. If clicked again it should release the point bearing and go back to light green with the bearing in the box goes back to live. The range button is a momentary switch. When depressed it will start the range recording and when released it stop the range recording, calculated the middle as the bearing and the uncertainty. Starting one mode automatically negates the previously recorded bearing. The point measurement just uses the standard uncertainty. Leave the pencil button to bring up the more detailed existing bearing measurement scree. Update the other record type screens as appropriate for consistency. Does this make sense? Any questions. I\'92m trying to simplify the bearing screen.\
